---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TechnicalPlate from "../../components/TechnicalPlate.astro";
import { fieldNotes } from "../../data/field-notes";
const incidents = fieldNotes.filter((note) => note.kind === "Factory incident");
---
<BaseLayout title="Incidents and factory learning" description="Incidents show what the factory believed, what failed, which control changed and what the lesson means elsewhere." path="/incidents/" image="/og/the-tests-passed.jpg">
  <section class="container page-intro">
    <div class="page-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">WOODHOUSE</a><span>/</span><span>Incidents</span></nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">The incident archive</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Make the next run safer.</h1>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-intro__aside"><strong>Belief → failure → evidence → control</strong>An incident is not a footnote. It is the record of what the factory had to change.</aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section paper-section">
    <div class="container">
      {incidents.map((note, index) => (
        <article class="ledger-note">
          <span class="ledger-note__index">INCIDENT / 0{index + 1}</span>
          <div class="ledger-note__main"><a href={"/dispatches/" + note.slug + "/"}><h2 class="ledger-note__title">{note.title}</h2></a><p class="ledger-note__deck">{note.deck}</p></div>
          <div class="ledger-note__side"><strong>{note.kind}</strong>{note.date}<br />{note.readingTime}</div>
        </article>
      ))}
      <p class="source-note"><strong>Method:</strong> the incident archive publishes reviewed lessons from project work. Private repository records are not reproduced.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="failure-patterns-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div><span class="section-index">Factory learning</span><h2 id="failure-patterns-title">Put the lesson in the next check.</h2></div>
        <p>The incident archive contains one published incident. The pattern register below collects risks in the reviewed project work. These are controls to keep, not six more incident reports.</p>
      </div>
      <TechnicalPlate
        id="failure-loop"
        number="03"
        title="Turn a failure into a control"
        variant="loop"
        note="The loop is only complete when the changed control is rerun against the same failure class and the result is recorded."
        steps={[
          { label: "Observe", title: "See the outcome", detail: "Use the real screen." },
          { label: "Trace", title: "Bind the claim", detail: "Use the exact revision." },
          { label: "Contain", title: "Limit the harm", detail: "Stop unsupported action." },
          { label: "Change", title: "Update the control", detail: "Fix gate or product." },
          { label: "Recheck", title: "Same failure class", detail: "Prove and record." }
        ]}
      />
      <div class="pattern-register">
        <div class="pattern-register__intro">
          <p class="eyebrow">AI and factory failure patterns</p>
          <h3>A confident answer can still be wrong.</h3>
          <p>The examples come from recurring project risks. Each one needs a control that survives the next run.</p>
        </div>
        <ol class="pattern-list">
          <li><strong>Confident invention at a source gap</strong><p>Leave unknowns visible. Require a source for each factual claim and keep expansion behind the parity gate.</p></li>
          <li><strong>Passing checks used to certify feel</strong><p>Tests can miss hierarchy, pacing and play quality. Inspect the screen in the real flow and intended viewport.</p></li>
          <li><strong>Old proof attached to new code</strong><p>Bind a result to the exact source or release, then repeat the check after a change.</p></li>
          <li><strong>One percentage hides changed scope</strong><p>Record what the denominator includes and when it changes. Name the work that remains.</p></li>
          <li><strong>Simulation stands in for people and hardware</strong><p>Software checks cannot prove the device, environment or human path. Observe each physical boundary directly.</p></li>
          <li><strong>Polish covers missing information</strong><p>Label promotional art, show the product state and next proof, and remove claims the source cannot support.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
